<article class="env-definition" id="00DZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00DZ">Definition <span data-tag="00DZ">10.17.1</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The <em>spectrum</em> of $R$ is the set of prime ideals of $R$. It is usually denoted $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Given a subset $T \subset R$ we let $V(T) \subset \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ be the set of primes containing $T$, i.e., $V(T) = \{  \mathfrak p \in \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R) \mid \forall f\in T, f\in \mathfrak p\} $. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Given an element $f \in R$ we let $D(f) \subset \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ be the set of primes not containing $f$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>